{% extends "base.html.jinja" %}
{% block content %}
<h1>{{ guide.h1 }}</h1>
<p class="lede">
  CDFW publishes a Fish Planting Schedule, and this site copies it into pages
  for each water, county and region. Here is what each part of it means.
  Every entry is scheduled, not confirmed (see
  <a href="{{ root }}guide/scheduled-vs-confirmed/">scheduled vs. confirmed</a>).
</p>

<h2 id="source">Where the schedule comes from</h2>
<p>
  CDFW describes its
  <a href="{{ cdfw_schedule_url }}">Fish Planting Schedule</a> as
  &ldquo;updated in real time, directly by CDFW Hatchery staff.&rdquo; This
  site reads that page once a day; it last did so {{ source_fetched_label }},
  when CDFW's current week was the {{ source_week_label }}. The
  <a href="{{ root }}support/#schedule">support page</a> and the
  <a href="{{ root }}about/#data">about page</a> say more.
</p>

<h2 id="weeks">Dates are weeks</h2>
<p>
  Every date on this site is a week, Sunday through Saturday, written as
  &ldquo;week of&rdquo; its Sunday. CDFW does not give a day. Its page says why:
  &ldquo;More specific dates are not given to avoid focusing excess fishing
  activity immediately after a plant.&rdquo; Calendar feeds from this site
  span the whole week for the same reason.
</p>

<h2 id="rows">What a row tells you</h2>
<p>
  A row names a water, the county or counties CDFW files it under, and a
  species. {{ water_count }} {{ "water is" if water_count == 1 else "waters are" }}
  in this site's record. A water that CDFW files under more than one county
  appears on each county's page. To see rows, start with
  <a href="{{ root }}">this week, statewide</a> or
  <a href="{{ root }}county/">pick a county</a>. Rows can also be read by species:
  {% for l in species_links %}<a href="{{ root }}species/{{ l.slug }}/">{{ l.name }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
</p>

<h2 id="regions">CDFW regions</h2>
<p>
  CDFW's schedule lets you filter by its six regions: Northern (R1), North
  Central (R2), Bay Delta (R3), Central (R4), South Coast (R5) and Inland
  Deserts (R6). This site has a page for each region that has a water on the
  schedule:
</p>
<ul class="water-index">
  {% for r in region_links %}
  <li><a href="{{ root }}region/{{ r.slug }}/">{{ r.name }}</a> <span class="muted">({{ r.county_count }} {{ "county" if r.county_count == 1 else "counties" }})</span></li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>

<h2 id="blank">What a blank week means</h2>
<p>
  If a water is not on the schedule for a week, no plant is scheduled for it
  that week, not that there are no fish. Each water page says so in similar
  words when nothing is current.
</p>

<h2 id="history">How far back it goes</h2>
<p>
  CDFW's page says it shows &ldquo;the current week, one week in the future,
  and six months in the past.&rdquo; This site keeps the weeks it has
  recorded{% if recorded_since_label %}, the earliest being the {{ recorded_since_label }}{% endif %},
  so a water page can list more weeks than CDFW's page does today. A week
  marked &ldquo;Schedule changed&rdquo; is one CDFW listed and later removed.
</p>

<h2 id="maps">Map locations</h2>
<p>
  CDFW notes that the map markers on its schedule show the general location
  of a water, not the exact or sole planting locations. Treat any map of a
  water the same way: it says roughly where the water is, not where fish are
  delivered. This site takes
  locations from federal data, described under
  <a href="{{ root }}about/#locations">water locations</a>.
</p>

<h2 id="questions">Questions about a plant</h2>
<p>
  CDFW's page asks that questions about fish planting go to the regional
  office that covers the area. It lists a number for each region. This site
  cannot answer them; it has no source beyond the schedule.
</p>

<h2>Keep reading</h2>
<ul>
  <li><a href="{{ root }}guide/scheduled-vs-confirmed/">Scheduled vs. confirmed</a></li>
  <li><a href="{{ root }}guide/what-is-a-trout-plant/">What is a trout plant?</a></li>
  <li><a href="{{ root }}guide/">All guides</a></li>
</ul>

<h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
<p class="muted">
  Quotations are from CDFW's
  <a href="{{ cdfw_schedule_url }}">Fish Planting Schedule</a>, fetched and
  read on {{ cdfw_read_on }}. Counts and dates come from this site's own
  record. This site is independent and is not affiliated with CDFW.
</p>
{% endblock %}
